The colour values in modus.css are copied from the Modus themes:

  modus-themes 5.3.0, https://github.com/protesilaos/modus-themes,
  commit c6a08aa1a8a70cc94eeb7939b26029187d5289f3, file modus-themes.el:
  modus-themes-operandi-tinted-palette (lines 1013-1338),
  modus-themes-vivendi-tinted-palette (lines 2319-2644) and
  modus-themes-common-palette-mappings (lines 534-677).

Each --modus- variable is a light-dark() pair of the operandi-tinted value
and the vivendi-tinted value. The named colours are copied as written; the
variables from cursor onward are Modus's semantic mappings, each resolved
by hand to the colour it names in each theme, a theme's own mapping taking
precedence over the common one. When modus-themes changes a colour, this
file is edited by hand from the new release.

